---
import GlassLayout from '../layouts/GlassLayout.astro';
---
<GlassLayout
  title="Why Study MBBS in Nepal — Honest Comparison for Indian Students | NepalMBBS.in"
  description="Why Indian students choose Nepal for MBBS: NMC recognition, no donation, English medium, proximity and cost compared with private colleges in India."
  path="/why-nepal"
>
<div class="tab-pane on" id="pane-why">
<div class="container">
  <div class="rev"><div class="eyebrow">Honest Comparison</div><div class="sec-title">Why Nepal MBBS — Facts Only</div><div class="sec-sub">No exaggeration. No false promises. Factual advantages verified from official NMC India and MEC Nepal sources only.</div></div>
  <div class="why-grid">
    <div class="why-card rev">
      <div class="why-img"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1469521669194-babb45599def?fm=webp&w=1400&q=95&fit=crop&auto=format&ixlib=rb-4.1.0" alt="Nepal Himalaya" loading="lazy"><div class="why-img-overlay"></div><div class="why-img-badge">✈️ No Visa Required</div></div>
      <div class="why-body"><h4>No visa required for Indian citizens</h4><p>India-Nepal bilateral open border agreement allows Indian citizens entry with just a valid passport or Aadhaar card. No visa process, no embassy visits required.</p></div>
    </div>
    <div class="why-card rev">
      <div class="why-img"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1576091160550-2173dba999ef?fm=webp&w=1400&q=95&fit=crop&auto=format&ixlib=rb-4.1.0" alt="Medical education" loading="lazy"><div class="why-img-overlay"></div><div class="why-img-badge">🏛️ NMC India Recognised</div></div>
      <div class="why-body"><h4>NMC India Recognised Colleges</h4><p>Select Nepal medical colleges are recognised by NMC India. Graduates from these colleges are eligible for NExT/FMGE. Always verify your specific college at nmc.org.in before applying.</p></div>
    </div>
    <div class="why-card rev">
      <div class="why-img"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1434030216411-0b793f4b4173?fm=webp&w=1400&q=95&fit=crop&auto=format&ixlib=rb-4.1.0" alt="Medical students studying" loading="lazy"><div class="why-img-overlay"></div><div class="why-img-badge">📚 India-Aligned Curriculum</div></div>
      <div class="why-body"><h4>India-Aligned MBBS Curriculum</h4><p>Nepal MBBS closely mirrors Indian MBBS syllabus — same core subjects, similar exam patterns. This directly aids NExT/FMGE preparation after graduation.</p></div>
    </div>
    <div class="why-card rev">
      <div class="why-img"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1523050854058-8df90110c9f1?fm=webp&w=1400&q=95&fit=crop&auto=format&ixlib=rb-4.1.0" alt="Students in Nepal" loading="lazy"><div class="why-img-overlay"></div><div class="why-img-badge">🗣️ English + Hindi</div></div>
      <div class="why-body"><h4>English Medium + Hindi Understood</h4><p>English is the medium of instruction per Nepal NMC. Hindi is widely spoken and understood in Nepal — no significant language barrier for Indian students in daily life.</p></div>
    </div>
    <div class="why-card rev">
      <div class="why-img"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1559757175-5700dde675bc?fm=webp&w=1400&q=95&fit=crop&auto=format&ixlib=rb-4.1.0" alt="Hospital clinical training" loading="lazy"><div class="why-img-overlay"></div><div class="why-img-badge">🏥 Clinical Exposure</div></div>
      <div class="why-body"><h4>Strong Clinical Exposure from Year 1</h4><p>Affiliated teaching hospitals provide hands-on patient exposure from early years. Disease patterns are similar to India — clinically relevant training for future Indian practice.</p></div>
    </div>
    <div class="why-card rev">
      <div class="why-img"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1571825304178-9e06ae61735c?fm=webp&w=1400&q=95&fit=crop&auto=format&ixlib=rb-4.1.0" alt="Kathmandu Nepal" loading="lazy"><div class="why-img-overlay"></div><div class="why-img-badge">🍛 Familiar Culture</div></div>
      <div class="why-body"><h4>Familiar Food, Culture & Community</h4><p>Indian food widely available in college hostels. Cultural similarities with India make daily life comfortable. Large Indian student community at all major Nepal colleges.</p></div>
    </div>
  </div>
  <!-- TESTIMONIALS -->
  <div style="margin-top:64px">
    <div class="tc rev"><div class="eyebrow">Student Stories</div><div class="sec-title">What Students Say</div><div class="sec-sub" style="margin:0 auto">Representative experiences. Individual experiences may vary. We recommend speaking directly with current students at your shortlisted college.</div></div>
    <div class="test-grid" id="testimonials-container">
      <div class="test-card rev"><div class="test-quote-icon">"</div><div class="test-stars">★★★★★</div><div class="test-text">The counseling was genuinely honest — they told me exactly what to expect, not just what I wanted to hear. MEC process was transparent and I got into my preferred college without any hassle.</div><div class="test-author"><div class="test-avatar">P</div><div><div class="test-name">Priya Sharma</div><div class="test-college">Mumbai → Kathmandu Medical College</div><span class="test-year">2nd Year MBBS</span></div></div></div>
      <div class="test-card rev"><div class="test-quote-icon">"</div><div class="test-stars">★★★★★</div><div class="test-text">NEET mein 380 tha. India mein private ka option bahut expensive tha. Nepal mein official MEC route se admission mila. Food, hostel sab manageable hai. Studies bhi achhi chal rahi hain.</div><div class="test-author"><div class="test-avatar">R</div><div><div class="test-name">Rahul Deshmukh</div><div class="test-college">Nagpur → KIST Medical College</div><span class="test-year">1st Year MBBS</span></div></div></div>
      <div class="test-card rev"><div class="test-quote-icon">"</div><div class="test-stars">★★★★★</div><div class="test-text">Parents were worried about safety. After visiting campus they felt comfortable. Hindi understood everywhere. Clinical exposure is genuinely strong from Year 1 — better than I expected.</div><div class="test-author"><div class="test-avatar">A</div><div><div class="test-name">Anjali Patil</div><div class="test-college">Pune → Gandaki Medical College</div><span class="test-year">3rd Year MBBS</span></div></div></div>
    </div>
    <p style="text-align:center;font-size:12px;color:var(--muted);font-style:italic;margin-top:16px">* Testimonials are representative. We recommend speaking with current students directly. Individual experiences may vary.</p>
  </div>
</div>
</div>
</GlassLayout>
